{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query manages caching by query key. Query keys must be arrays at the top level, and they should uniquely describe the data returned by the query function."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"simple-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simple Keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use simple keys for list resources or non-hierarchical data:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"createQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['settings'],\n  queryFn: fetchSettings,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keys-with-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keys with Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Include variables when they change what the query fetches:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"createQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['projects', { page: this.page, filter: this.filter }],\n  queryFn: () => fetchProjects({ page: this.page, filter: this.filter }),\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pagination example uses a key shaped like this:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ProjectsQueryKey = readonly ['projects', number, number, boolean]\n\nfunction projectsQueryKey(\n  page: number,\n  delayMs: number,\n  forceError: boolean,\n): ProjectsQueryKey {\n  return ['projects', page, delayMs, forceError] as const\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"deterministic-hashing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deterministic Hashing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Object key order does not matter inside a query key:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const keyA = ['todos', { status, page }]\nconst keyB = ['todos', { page, status }]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array item order does matter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const keyA = ['todos', status, page]\nconst keyB = ['todos', page, status]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"query-keys-as-dependencies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Keys as Dependencies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your query function reads a reactive host property, include that value in the query key:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"class UserTodos extends LitElement {\n  userId = ''\n\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, () => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos', this.userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(this.userId),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This lets Lit Query cache each user's todos separately and refetch when the host state changes."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"simple-keys","text":"Simple Keys","level":2},{"id":"keys-with-variables","text":"Keys with Variables","level":2},{"id":"deterministic-hashing","text":"Deterministic Hashing","level":2},{"id":"query-keys-as-dependencies","text":"Query Keys as Dependencies","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Query manages caching by query key. Query keys must be arrays at the top level, and they should uniquely describe the data returned by the query function.\n\n## Simple Keys\n\nUse simple keys for list resources or non-hierarchical data:\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['settings'],\n  queryFn: fetchSettings,\n})\n```\n\n## Keys with Variables\n\nInclude variables when they change what the query fetches:\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['projects', { page: this.page, filter: this.filter }],\n  queryFn: () => fetchProjects({ page: this.page, filter: this.filter }),\n}))\n```\n\nThe pagination example uses a key shaped like this:\n\n```ts\ntype ProjectsQueryKey = readonly ['projects', number, number, boolean]\n\nfunction projectsQueryKey(\n  page: number,\n  delayMs: number,\n  forceError: boolean,\n): ProjectsQueryKey {\n  return ['projects', page, delayMs, forceError] as const\n}\n```\n\n## Deterministic Hashing\n\nObject key order does not matter inside a query key:\n\n```ts\nconst keyA = ['todos', { status, page }]\nconst keyB = ['todos', { page, status }]\n```\n\nArray item order does matter:\n\n```ts\nconst keyA = ['todos', status, page]\nconst keyB = ['todos', page, status]\n```\n\n## Query Keys as Dependencies\n\nIf your query function reads a reactive host property, include that value in the query key:\n\n```ts\nclass UserTodos extends LitElement {\n  userId = ''\n\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, () => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos', this.userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(this.userId),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\nThis lets Lit Query cache each user's todos separately and refetch when the host state changes.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-keys\ntitle: Query Keys\n---\n\nTanStack Query manages caching by query key. Query keys must be arrays at the top level, and they should uniquely describe the data returned by the query function.\n\n## Simple Keys\n\nUse simple keys for list resources or non-hierarchical data:\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['settings'],\n  queryFn: fetchSettings,\n})\n```\n\n## Keys with Variables\n\nInclude variables when they change what the query fetches:\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['projects', { page: this.page, filter: this.filter }],\n  queryFn: () => fetchProjects({ page: this.page, filter: this.filter }),\n}))\n```\n\nThe pagination example uses a key shaped like this:\n\n```ts\ntype ProjectsQueryKey = readonly ['projects', number, number, boolean]\n\nfunction projectsQueryKey(\n  page: number,\n  delayMs: number,\n  forceError: boolean,\n): ProjectsQueryKey {\n  return ['projects', page, delayMs, forceError] as const\n}\n```\n\n## Deterministic Hashing\n\nObject key order does not matter inside a query key:\n\n```ts\nconst keyA = ['todos', { status, page }]\nconst keyB = ['todos', { page, status }]\n```\n\nArray item order does matter:\n\n```ts\nconst keyA = ['todos', status, page]\nconst keyB = ['todos', page, status]\n```\n\n## Query Keys as Dependencies\n\nIf your query function reads a reactive host property, include that value in the query key:\n\n```ts\nclass UserTodos extends LitElement {\n  userId = ''\n\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, () => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos', this.userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodos(this.userId),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\nThis lets Lit Query cache each user's todos separately and refetch when the host state changes.\n"}
